`SafeAreaEdges="None"` only tells the page not to inset content for safe areas — it doesn't make the system bars transparent or allow drawing behind them. You need **platform-specific setup** too:

### Android — enable edge-to-edge in `MainActivity.cs`

```csharp
protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    if (Window is not null)
    {
        Window.SetStatusBarColor(Android.Graphics.Color.Transparent);
        Window.SetNavigationBarColor(Android.Graphics.Color.Transparent);

        // Draw behind system bars
        WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window, false);
    }
}
```

> You'll need `using AndroidX.Core.View;` for `WindowCompat`.
> On Android 15+ (API 35), edge-to-edge is enforced automatically, but you still need transparent bars.

### iOS — confirm safe area is fully ignored

On the XAML page, combine both:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns:ios="clr-namespace:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.PlatformConfiguration.iOSSpecific;assembly=Microsoft.Maui.Controls"
             ios:Page.UseSafeArea="False">
```

`SafeAreaEdges="None"` and `UseSafeArea="False"` serve similar purposes; make sure at least one is set.

### Your Image

Use `Aspect="AspectFill"` so the image scales to cover the full area:

```xml
<Image Source="photo.jpg"
       Aspect="AspectFill"
       HorizontalOptions="Fill"
       VerticalOptions="Fill" />
```

**TL;DR**: The missing piece is almost certainly the Android side — you need `WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window, false)` plus transparent system bar colors.
